                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Phoenix AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 30 at 9:10PM MST until October 30 at 10:45PM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ",
                "description": "At 910 PM MST, Local law enforcement reported multiple water rescues\nwithin the warned area. Between 0.75 and 2.25 inches of rain have\nfallen. Flooding impacts will continue, but no additional rainfall is\nexpected.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Law enforcement reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams, urban\nareas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nPhoenix, Paradise Valley, Piestewa Peak Park, Camelback Mountain\nand Arizona State Fairgrounds.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
